    "created_at": "2023-01-24T18:11:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-24T18:11:21Z",
    "body": "I was [actioned](https://www.w3.org/International/track/actions/1234) by the I18N WG with looking into this issue and it's friend whatwg/html#8728. \r\n\r\nOur tendency as a WG is to agree that it would be nice to have a `<meta charaset=\"utf-8\">` in the \"basic example\" in the introduction, but in my investigation of the current state of character encoding handling in the HTML suite of specs and in re-reading the introduction, I can see how introducing this nicety would be a distraction. I support closing this issue and 8728 and have marked our i18n-activity mirror issues for close.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
